Seed: the range and set element parsers read the current culture instead of the invariant one, so a literal read under de-DE refuses the decimal bound -1.5 (or, with a group separator, reads another number) while every explicit provider is still ignored
Oracles: CultureEntryPointProbeTests, HostCultureProbeTests
Fails: Parse, TryParse, TypeConverter, configuration and JSON reads under de-DE, sv-SE, fa-IR and th-TH for the integer and decimal ranges, multiranges and sets; the host answers 400 to a valid literal under those request cultures
History: LiteralProviderContractTests varies only the provider, with the current culture left as the machine sets it, so it catches this only on a machine whose own culture is not invariant

